# English

**SpaceMaster for Jellyfin — Third-party room-acoustics correction layer.**

This document explains how this project relates to Jellyfin, ffmpeg and other open-source
components regarding copyright, trademark and licensing. The compliance principles below apply
to **both** installation variants: "Version A (you already have Jellyfin)" and
"Version B (you don't have Jellyfin)".

### 1. Nature of the project
SpaceMaster is a **third-party** add-on for the Jellyfin media server. It is **not** an official
Jellyfin product and **not** a modified distribution of Jellyfin.

### 2. Jellyfin copyright (GPLv2+)
Jellyfin and its components (including the jellyfin-ffmpeg shipped in its image) are licensed
under the **GNU General Public License v2 or later (GPLv2+)**.

- This project does **not modify** Jellyfin's source or binaries;
- This project does **not redistribute** Jellyfin. End users obtain Jellyfin from the official
  Docker Hub image `jellyfin/jellyfin` (or other official Jellyfin channels); that distribution
  and its GPL source obligation are handled by the **Jellyfin project itself**;
- Jellyfin source: <https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin>
- jellyfin-ffmpeg source: <https://github.com/jellyfin/jellyfin-ffmpeg>

If you need Jellyfin's corresponding source (as required by the GPL), go to the official
repositories above. **We (SpaceMaster) neither hold nor distribute Jellyfin's source**, because
it is outside our distribution scope.

### 3. Trademark
"Jellyfin" is a trademark of the Jellyfin project. References to "Jellyfin" in this project's
name and docs are **descriptive only**, indicating compatibility. SpaceMaster is **not affiliated
with, endorsed by, or sponsored by** the Jellyfin project. Any implication of official association
is expressly disclaimed.

### 4. ffmpeg / jellyfin-ffmpeg (GPL)
Our `sm_wrapper.sh` only **intercepts** Jellyfin's invocation of ffmpeg: it does **not alter
ffmpeg's code**; it merely injects the filter arguments (computed by our engine) into the **same**
ffmpeg transcode. The ffmpeg that actually runs is the original one shipped by the official
Jellyfin image.

### 5. Closed-source engine `sm_dsp_engine` (separate process · not a derivative work)
The proprietary acoustic algorithms (room-mode derivation, PEQ, downmix matrix, symmetric
surround delay, balance) ship as a compiled native binary `sm_dsp_engine`; its source
`engine_core.py` is **not published**.

- The binary runs as a **separate process** (fork/exec of the real ffmpeg) via `sm_wrapper.sh` —
  an independent program that merely aggregates at runtime with Jellyfin / ffmpeg;
- It is **not a derivative work** of Jellyfin or ffmpeg (GPL components);
- Therefore its closed-source status **imposes no obligations** on Jellyfin's / ffmpeg's GPL
  terms, and it is **not forced open** by the GPL;
- Conversely, the GPL of Jellyfin / ffmpeg **does not extend** to this closed-source binary.

This is the classic "mere aggregation / independent programs cooperating via system calls" case,
distinct from "statically/dynamically linking a GPL library" which would create a derivative work.

### 6. Open-source spirit: the integration layer is fully open
Everything in this public repository — shell wrappers, console UI, Docker files, config formats,
docs — is **open source**, freely auditable, modifiable and redistributable. We keep only the
proprietary acoustic algorithm closed (as a compiled binary), as deliberate IP protection that
does **not** prevent users from auditing the integration mechanics.

### 7. Both install variants are compliant (Version A / Version B)

| Variant | Description | Where Jellyfin comes from |
|---------|-------------|---------------------------|
| **Version A** (you already have Jellyfin) | Use your existing Jellyfin; only let our wrapper/engine take over its ffmpeg | your **own existing** Jellyfin |
| **Version B** (you don't have Jellyfin) | `docker-compose.yml` has your Docker **pull the official `jellyfin/jellyfin`**, then mounts our engine | official Docker Hub image |

In both cases, **Jellyfin is always obtained by you / Docker Hub; SpaceMaster never hosts or
redistributes Jellyfin**.

### 8. Disclaimer
This project is provided "as-is", without warranty of any kind. Use of this project to modify
Jellyfin's transcode pipeline is at your own risk.
